    "cache mode: cold-warm — per task and arm, repeat 1 is cold and repeats 2..2 are warm (sessions carry cache_phase; aggregate.by_phase compares them)",
    "cold sessions (repeat 1): new fixture copy, HOME, TMPDIR and empty CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR per session; per-session nonce first in --append-system-prompt; only the MCP servers on the command line; prompt caching ON as in real Claude Code use (no DISABLE_PROMPT_CACHING). First-call cache reads are not enforced to 0: Claude Code's built-in system prompt and tool definitions are identical in every session, so that static prefix can be read from cache; the nonce and fresh paths stop any match beyond it. 8032 cached tokens read on first calls (all arms, cold sessions); cache writes (cache_write) are the honest cold cost and count as uncached tokens",
    "warm sessions (repeats 2..N): fresh fixture copy and HOME at the cold session’s paths, the cold session’s nonce and index reused (copied, not rebuilt), same args and env as cold; first-call cache reads expected and not checked",
